{
    "background_story": "Nori was a young monk who lived in a remote monastery nestled in the mountains. He was known for his reverent nature, displaying deep respect and devotion to the ancient traditions and teachings of his order. Nori spent most of his days studying sacred texts, meditating, and practicing intricate rituals. His reverence was not limited to his faith, but extended to the natural world around him. He would often take long walks in the forest, pausing to admire the beauty of a sunrise or the tranquility of a waterfall. The other monks looked up to Nori as a role model, inspired by his humility and dedication. As he tended to the monastery's gardens, Nori would whisper prayers, believing that every seed he planted and every flower he nurtured was a sacred act. His reverent spirit brought peace and harmony to all those around him.",
